  "details": "I notice that for some reason this already exists for worlds, but not for avatars?\n\nAnyway, we already have this feature in the SDK now, for both worlds *and* avatars, allowing us to make edits without reuploading the asset, which I appreciate.\n\nNow I'd love to see it also on the website, so that we don't even have to launch Unity to make these changes.\n\nI basically just want the website to come to parity to the same level of control that the content manager in the SDK has.\n\nYou already have support for most of the features that the content manager has, it just needs to allow editing of names, descriptions, and tags, and that'd be that.\n\nThanks.\n\nOther relevant, but not quite as specific/current, posts:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/allow-organizing-avatars-from-the-vrchat-website\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/allow-the-editing-of-avatar-and-world-names-descriptions-after-uploading",
